--TEST--
A `?T` parameter of a `Core` member takes the mark its row gives `T`, so a `tainted` argument reaches `Core\Path::withExtension` and the mark travels to its result — `rule:security/unclassified-parameter-refuses-tainted`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Path::withExtension
// `withExtension`'s `?string $extension` is contagious, so the mark travels to
// the result and a `tainted string` variable is where it has to go. A `?T` that
// dropped the mark would refuse the call at compile time.
tainted string $extension = "csv";
tainted string $renamed = Core\Path::withExtension("report.txt", $extension);
echo "renamed: ", Core\Str::length($renamed), " characters\n";
--EXPECT--
renamed: 10 characters
